# Plan Learning Packs

This is the routing-only planning runtime call for current-code learning. Identify high-value input files and build self-contained evidence packs for their decision-bearing boundaries. The deterministic learning pipeline completes coverage for input files that are not assigned here; do not spend output on a path-by-path inventory. Do not inspect source bodies or call MCP, CodeGraph, or other repository tools in this planning pass; source-body verification belongs to isolated pack analysis.

Project:
- name: {{.ProjectName}}
- path: {{.RootPath}}
- language: {{.Language}}
- learning mode: {{.LearningMode}}

Learning strategy guidance:
- `fast`: reduce exploration cost and plan only the clearest boundaries.
- `normal`: use the default high-precision planning bar.
- `deep`: inspect more connected paths before deciding; it does not create packs for weak or merely local observations.
- The mode changes exploration breadth only. It is not a fixed count, file budget, or permission to invent weak packs.
- Treat the agenda as a compact set of review batches, not a taxonomy of every capability. Consolidate neighboring responsibilities when they share the same future change boundary and evidence can be verified together. Before returning, merge overlapping or duplicate boundaries; keep a focus separate only when it has an independent high-risk or externally observable decision boundary. Never create one focus per file, package, service, technical lane, or symbol family.

